# Beacon app (`src/ui/`, `src/app/`)

- The app is Preact + TypeScript in `src/ui/`, bundled by `scripts/build.mjs` into `src/app/build/app.js` and `app.css` (target `firefox84`). `src/app/index.html` loads only those two files; `src/app/build/` is build output.
- Folders: `app/` (router, focus, hooks, theme), `components/` (shared building blocks; `components/chat/` holds the chat bubbles, message options, and the `useChatSession`/`useChatComposer`/`useChatKeys` hooks), `screens/` (one screen or a small family per file; `screens/settings/` holds the settings sub-screens), `data/` (`store.ts` barrel over `data/store/`, `normalize.ts` over `data/normalize/`, ws, db, config, http, attachments, platform), `theme/` (CSS). Import through the barrels (`data/store`, `screens/Chat`, `screens/Settings`); put new code in the module behind them.
- Target Gecko 84: no CSS `:has()`, no container queries, nothing newer than ES2020 at runtime.
- Screens are function components opened with `router.push(Screen, props)`. Menus and dialogs are overlays from `components/Overlays.tsx`: `showOptions` for an options menu (separate groups of related items with `DIVIDER`), and `confirm`, `alertDialog`, `prompt`, `pick`, `pickMany`, which resolve a promise with the answer. Don't build ad-hoc popups.
- Declare softkeys with `useSoftkeys` and keys with `useKeys` (return `true` to stop propagation). Lists use `RowList` or `useListNav`, so D-pad focus and scroll behave the same everywhere.
- Re-render from the store with `useStoreEvents`; don't poll.
- Every user-facing string lives in `S` in `src/ui/strings.ts`, written for someone who has never heard of Signal's protocol. Terms such as PreKey, ACI, PNI, device ID, registration ID, sessions, WebSocket, or envelope belong only in `DEBUG` and the Settings > Debug screen. `test/ui-wording.test.ts` enforces this.
- Turn caught errors into wording with `friendlyError(err)` or `sendError(err)` from `src/ui/errors.ts`; they log the detail with `dbg`. Never show `err.message` to the user.
- Preact escapes text, so render untrusted content as children or through `RichText`. Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- Log with `dbg(msg, data)` from `data/log.ts`. Use `toast(msg)` for transient notices.
- Reach KaiOS B2G APIs (activities, alarms, device storage, notifications) only through `data/platform.ts`.
- Talk to Signal through `signal` from `data/api.ts`; HTTP goes through `data/http.ts`.
- `data/ws.ts` ACKs an envelope only after decrypt and persistence succeed; keep it that way.
- Keep the upgrade keys from 2.0.x: the origin `signal4kaios`, the `s4k.config` localStorage key, the `signal4kaios:<number>` databases, the `s4k-wake` alarm and cache, and `/__s4k_pending_conv`.
- The privileged CSP forbids inline handlers, inline `<script>`/`<style>`, `eval`, and `new Function`; `scripts/package.sh` fails the build on `eval(`. Preact's `style={{...}}` is fine (it sets CSSOM properties).
- `src/app/vendor/*.wasm` and `src/app/build/` are build output; edit `src/ui/`, `src/engine/`, or `src/native/` instead. Edit `src/app/assets/icons/beacon.svg` and run `npm run icons` for the launcher icons.

```tsx
// Good
useSoftkeys({ left: S.newChat, center: S.open, right: S.options });
toast(friendlyError(err));
// Bad: technical wording in everyday UI
toast('PreKey upload failed: ' + err.message);
```
